./LOGBOOK.md:20:- AUTHORITY: The owner confirmed an authenticated Apple Developer session for Relux Works, LLC and authority for revision `2026-07-28.r12`: exactly the four macOS App IDs, Network Extensions on all four, and one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Apple-silicon Mac registered. No App Group record/capability, Keychain access-group portal mutation, iOS App ID, distribution profile, or `works.relux.proxy` change is authorized.
./LOGBOOK.md:182:- ROOT CAUSE: r6 built rule **S1** so every cross-platform *summary* sentence is a checked projection of the target rows. It left `verification.assertions` — the **other** prose projection of the same rows — unchecked. Two assertions were already stale under it: **A5** claimed `application-groups` on *every* iOS bundle (r5 prohibited both iOS probe rows) and **A9** claimed *every* development profile carries this Mac (all four iOS profile rows declare `devices = ["deferred — ADR-024"]`). Verdict 07 F1/F2. The 1024-check r7 validator passed because **R27 compared assertion membership and substrings, never scope against the rows**.
