5G Network Slicing
5G network slicing enables your apps to access dedicated segments of carrier networks to deliver higher levels of performance and quality of service for eligible categories of applications and traffic.
A Boolean value indicating whether to match the driver against devices that communicate using networking protocols.
A Boolean value indicating whether your app may use low-latency wireless networking.
A Boolean value that indicates whether the app may, with the user’s permission, access app and website usage information from the current device.
A Boolean value that indicates whether the driver communicates with human interface devices.
A Boolean value that indicates whether the driver creates a virtual HID device.
A Boolean value that indicates whether to match the driver against devices with serial communication interfaces.
Access Wi-Fi Information allows an app to obtain information about the currently connected Wi-Fi network or hotspot using the NEHotspotNetwork framework.
Accessory Transport Extension provides a secure channel for an authorized third-party accessory using the AccessorySetupKit framework to access approved data from a user's device.
Add Devices to Automated Device Enrollment allows an app to integrate Apple Configurator for iPhone's feature to scan and add iOS and macOS devices to an organization in Apple School Manager, Apple Business Manager or Apple Business Essentials.
Allow or deny network connections.
Allows an app to communicate with the same app on one or more other devices to create a group activity within a FaceTime call.
Allows your app to participate in the process of authenticating with hotspot networks.
App Identifier Entitlement for Marzipan profiles
Application Identifier Entitlement for Marzipan enabled profiles
Application Identifier Entitlement for OS Data Transfer enabled profiles
Carrier-Constrained Network - App Category
Carrier-Constrained Network Category and Optimized
Carrier-constrained networking entitlements enable your app to define its app category for accessing a carrier-provided satellite network, and indicating whether it’s optimized for such a network.
Configure settings for network relays.
Custom Network Protocol
Custom Network Protocol Entitlement
Data protection allows an app that accesses sensitive user data to use the built-in encryption available on some devices.
DriverKit Family Networking
DriverKit Family Networking (development)
DriverKit Family Networking for development
DriverKit Networking
Enable the Alternative App Marketplace entitlement to support installation of authorized applications onto eligible devices.
Enable your application or app extension to discover the current user of the device.
Enables access to user's personalized spatial audio profile.
Enables an app to claim exclusive ownership of a connected USB accessory, allowing direct communication with the device without sharing access with other processes.
Enables an app to exceed the default app memory limit on supported devices.
Enables an app to inspect the system's active network connections and the hardware addresses of nearby network resources, allowing network management and observability tools to report accurate connection state.
Enables an app to interact with a local thread network to access and manage credentials to interact with hardware on the network.
Enables background processing via GPU on supported devices
Enabling Custom Network Protocol allows your app to use custom network protocols that run on top of IP, or use custom network protocols that run on top of the network link layer.
Enrollment Single Sign On reduces the number of sign ins required during enrollment into device management by installing a managed version of your app and using it to authenticate throughout the flow.
Head Pose allows apps to use framework methods that access a user's head pose on capable devices.
HealthKit Estimate Recalibration allows an app to tell the device to recalibrate its estimates for specified sample types.
Hotspot configurations allow an app to configure Wi-Fi networks.
Indicates that your app is optimized for a carrier-provided satellite network
Manage Thread Network Credentials
Manage Thread Network Credentials (Development)
Manage Thread Network Credentials (development)
Multicast Networking
Network Extensions
Network Extensions Entitlement
Network Slicing app category
Network Slicing app traffic
Network Topology Observation
Persistent Content Capture grants software the ability to always capture frames from the device once a user has approved a single time.
Proxy TCP and UDP network connections.
Push notifications use the Apple Push Notifications service (APNs) to deliver notifications to devices.
Sensitive Content Analysis allows an app to detect sensitive images and videos that contain nudity on-device for the intended purposes of allowing users to choose to view the photo before showing it to them, or a heavier weight intervention.
Sustained Execution indicates whether your app can exhibit consistent, sustained performance when the system constrains the app to lower power levels on applicable devices.
Tap to Share lets merchants use their iPhone to connect to a customer's device with a simple NFC tap, enabling seamless data exchange at checkout. Customers can share contact details for membership sign-up, provide a shipping address or email for digital receipts, add or share Wallet passes, view their itemized cart, and pay with Apple Pay. Tap to Share requires an active Tap to Pay on iPhone session.
The DL-TDoA entitlement only supports development builds and Ad Hoc testing.
The HCE entitlement allows access to an iOS device’s NFC controller using host card emulation (HCE) for in-store NFC transactions in the European Economic Area (EEA).
The network extensions capability allows app extensions to extend and customize the networking capabilities of a device.
This allows the app to tell the device to recalibrate its estimates for specified sample types.
This entitlement enables wireless carrier apps to detect if a user's device has a SIM or eSIM installed associated to an individual carrier. This ability is to support carrier specific features and services by verifying that the device is using their own wireless carrier.
This entitlement works with DL-TDoA ranging feature in Nearby Interaction framework, which provides information from a Downlink Time-Difference-of-Arrival network.
This entitlement works with the EnergyKit framework, which provides insights and suggestions to manage home device electricity usage.
This is an arbitrary alphanumeric string that is associated with the device as an identifier. For example, you can find the name of an iOS device in the General > About settings.
To request permanent pairing access of a new device authorized or paired using DeviceDiscoveryUI you must set this entitlement to “permanent”
To use this DL-TDoA SDK, add this entitlement to your app by enabling the Nearby Interaction DL-TDoA capability on your target in Xcode.
Tunnel IP packets using a tunneling network protocol.
Use DriverKit to create device drivers that the user installs on their Mac.
VMNet indicates whether the app manages virtual network interfaces without escalating privileges to the root user.
Web Browser Engine Networking 
Web Browser Engine Networking entitlement
When a user enables critical alert notifications, your app can send push notifications that play a sound at an app-specified volume when the device is locked, muted, or has Do Not Disturb enabled.
Wi-Fi Network Sharing
Wi-Fi Network Sharing allows an app to share information about connected Wi-Fi networks with accessories using the AccessorySetupKit framework.
