- FINDING: A full-duplex echo can legitimately cross the per-direction byte threshold twice—once for sent protected bytes and again for received protected bytes. The byte-threshold regression therefore uses bounded one-directional exec/stdin traffic to prove one exact trigger without weakening the per-direction policy or hiding a second valid KEX.
- VERIFICATION: Five focused byte-trigger stress runs and three consecutive complete `swift test --filter LibSSH2` runs pass (44 tests/3 suites each). `make validate-core` passes 378 tests/31 suites plus boundary/build checks; pinned libssh2/rekey, source-tamper, dual-architecture macOS provider/harness, strict Swift format, and diff gates all exit 0. Board validation exits 0 while continuing to report the known story aggregate mismatch.

